---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageBanner from '../components/PageBanner.astro';
import { ACCESSIBILITY, HERO_RULES, shown } from '../data/classic';
import { GAME } from '../config';
import { url } from '../lib';

const abilities = [
  { name: 'Move', text: 'Walk, aim, crouch and climb.' },
  { name: 'Jump', text: 'Jump, and swim. OK in menus.' },
  { name: 'Attack', text: 'Each hero’s attack; hold it to run. Back in menus.' },
  { name: 'Special', text: 'Each hero’s special weapon or move.' },
  { name: 'Tools', text: 'Each hero’s extra tool or weapon swap. Back in menus.' },
  { name: 'Pause / Menu', text: 'Pause the game and open its menu. OK in menus.' },
];
---

<Base title="How to play" description="How to play Super Mario Bros. Crossover: REMIX: getting started, controls on keyboard, gamepad and touch, and the accessibility options.">
  <PageBanner title="How to play" intro="Keyboard, gamepad or touch: the game switches between them as you use them." />
  <div class="wrap page">
    <section aria-labelledby="start">
      <h2 id="start">Getting started</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><a href={GAME.playUrl}>Open the game</a> (or <a href={url('play/')}>play it in this site's page</a>).</li>
        <li>On the title screen, pick <strong>Classic</strong>.</li>
        <li>Pick a map set, then a hero. Each hero plays their own way: <a href={url('heroes/')}>see how</a>.</li>
        <li>
          In a level, <strong>Pause</strong> opens the menu, where <strong>Guide</strong> shows the moves of the hero you're
          playing. <strong>Options → How to play</strong> on the title screen has every Classic hero's guide.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Sound starts on your first press or tap. The game saves your settings and progress in your browser.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="heroes">
      <h2 id="heroes">Choosing a hero</h2>
      <ul>
        {shown(HERO_RULES).map((r) => <li>{r.text}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p><a href={url('heroes/')}>Meet the heroes</a> and watch each one play.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="abilities">
      <h2 id="abilities">Abilities</h2>
      <p>
        Every hero has the same abilities; what they do changes from hero to hero. Every screen and prompt names the
        ability, not the key, and <strong>Options → Controls</strong> lists your keys and pad buttons.
      </p>
      <dl class="defs panel">
        {
          abilities.map((a) => (
            <div>
              <dt>{a.name}</dt>
              <dd>{a.text}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="devices">
      <h2 id="devices">Keyboard, gamepad and touch</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Keyboard and gamepad:</strong> both work out of the box, and every ability can be remapped on either.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Touch:</strong> an on-screen pad, set to Auto, On or Off, with a fixed d-pad or a floating stick and an
          adjustable size. The buttons are captioned with your hero's moves (SWORD, MISSILE, RUSH). On the hero select, tap
          a hero to move there and tap again to pick.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Phones and tablets</strong> can add the game to the Home Screen: open it with <em>Play</em>, then use
          the browser's Share or menu button and <em>Add to Home Screen</em>. It then opens like an app, full screen.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="access">
      <h2 id="access">Accessibility options</h2>
      <p>In <strong>Options</strong> on the title screen (Video, Audio and Controls).</p>
      <dl class="defs">
        {
          ACCESSIBILITY.map((a) => (
            <div>
              <dt>{a.name}</dt>
              <dd>{a.text}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
      <p>
        Unlocked cheats (Invincible, Infinite Lives, Infinite Time, Extra Checkpoints, Level Select) and More settings
        (Lives, When hit) can make the game easier: see <a href={url('modes/')}>Maps &amp; modes</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The rules the game follows for every screen, card and menu are written down in its{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/jelloshooter848/SMBC/blob/main/docs/ACCESSIBILITY.md">accessibility rules</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="saves">
      <h2 id="saves">Keeping your saves</h2>
      <p>
        The game saves to your browser. To keep your progress safe, or to carry it to another device, open{' '}
        <strong>Options → Save data</strong> on the title screen:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Back up on device</strong> exports everything (saves, settings, progress and custom levels) to one
          backup file, and <strong>Import backup</strong> brings it back. This is the safest way to keep your game.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Back up online</strong> saves an encrypted copy on five free <a href="https://nostr.com/">Nostr</a>{' '}
          servers and gives you a 12-character backup code, like <code>ABCD-EF12-3456</code>. There's no account: the
          code is the key. Use <strong>Restore from code</strong> to bring the copy back on any device, and back up
          again with the same code to update it. <strong>Delete most recent code</strong> asks the servers to delete it.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The servers see only an anonymous ID and when you backed up, nothing personal. Online backup is experimental,
        and free servers may lose data, so keep a backup file too. Keep your code private: anyone with it can restore
        your saves. The offline copy has no online backup.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="offline">
      <h2 id="offline">Playing offline</h2>
      <p>
        Download the offline zip from the <a href={url('versions/#offline')}>downloads</a>, unzip it, and open its{' '}
        <code>index.html</code>. No install and no internet needed.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page section {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .page li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .defs > div + div {
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
  }
  .defs dt {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .defs dd {
    margin: 0.2rem 0 0;
  }
</style>
